    "description": "<h2>Overview</h2>\n<p>Initial research release of the N-Body Gravitational Integration Benchmark, a Python project for investigating numerical methods used to integrate gravitational N-body systems.</p>\n<h2>Numerical methods</h2>\n<p>This release includes implementations of:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forward Euler</li>\n<li>Velocity-Verlet</li>\n<li>Classical fourth-order Runge-Kutta (RK4)</li>\n<li>Fourth-order Yoshida symplectic integration</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Benchmark systems</h2>\n<p>The project examines gravitational systems including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sun\u2013Earth</li>\n<li>Sun\u2013Earth\u2013Mars</li>\n<li>Binary systems</li>\n<li>Eccentric Kepler orbits</li>\n<li>The figure-eight three-body problem</li>\n<li>Random gravitational clusters</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Numerical diagnostics</h2>\n<p>The benchmark framework examines energy conservation, angular momentum conservation, trajectory accuracy, and numerical convergence.</p>\n<h2>Research materials</h2>\n<p>The release includes the project source files, supporting benchmark results, figures, and research manuscript.</p>\n<h2>Reproducibility</h2>\n<p>See <code>README.md</code> for project documentation and instructions. Dependencies are listed in <code>requirements.txt</code>.</p>\n<h2>Version</h2>\n<p>v1.0.0 \u2014 Initial research release.</p>",
